
This directory is intended for PlatformIO Test Runner and project tests.

Browser firmware-update detection has a Node.js host test:

```sh
node test/host/test_firmware_reload.js
```

Unit Testing is a software testing method by which individual units of
source code, sets of one or more MCU program modules together with associated
control data, usage procedures, and operating procedures, are tested to
determine whether they are fit for use. Unit testing finds problems early
in the development cycle.

More information about PlatformIO Unit Testing:
- https://docs.platformio.org/en/latest/advanced/unit-testing/index.html

The mesh session state has a host-side test. On a machine with a C++17 compiler, run:

```sh
g++ -std=c++17 -Iinclude test/host/test_mesh_fx_session.cpp -o test_mesh_fx_session
./test_mesh_fx_session
```

The mesh HTTP tests compile the production receiver, JSON codec, and sender
against fake HTTP/FreeRTOS services. They exercise acknowledgments, lost replies,
bounded retries, heartbeat expiry, queue-full recovery, stale/duplicate state,
master restarts, sequence/timer rollover, sleep-safe snapshots, and opt-out:

```sh
g++ -std=c++17 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -Itest/host/mesh_stubs -Iinclude -I.pio/libdeps/rp2040-rel/ArduinoJson/src src/mesh_http.cpp test/host/test_mesh_http.cpp -o test_mesh_http
./test_mesh_http
g++ -std=c++17 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -Itest/host/mesh_stubs -Iinclude -I.pio/libdeps/rp2040-rel/ArduinoJson/src -Ilib/Utils/src src/mesh_http.cpp src/mesh_sender.cpp test/host/test_mesh_sender.cpp -o test_mesh_sender
./test_mesh_sender
g++ -std=c++17 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -DIGNORE_WEB_EFFECT_CHANGES=1 -Itest/host/mesh_stubs -Iinclude -I.pio/libdeps/rp2040-rel/ArduinoJson/src src/mesh_http.cpp test/host/test_mesh_http.cpp -o test_mesh_ignored
./test_mesh_ignored
```

For RP2350, substitute `rp2350-rel` in the ArduinoJson include path. A mixed-board
hardware run is still needed to verify radio loss, reconnection, and overnight
restoration on actual devices.

Board UID selection, runtime buffer sizing, and allocation rollback have a host-side test:

```sh
g++ -std=c++17 -Iinclude src/board_config.cpp test/host/test_board_config.cpp -o test_board_config
./test_board_config
```

OTA upload authorization, cleanup, short writes, staging failures, image locking,
and reboot signalling have host-side tests using the production upload and reboot code:

```sh
g++ -std=c++17 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -Itest/host/ota_stubs -Iinclude -Ilib/FilesystemTask/src src/ota_upload.cpp src/ota_upgrade.cpp test/host/test_ota.cpp -o test_ota
./test_ota
```

The OTA stubs provide fake files, PicoOTA commands, HTTP callbacks, and watchdog
resets. A board test is still required to exercise WiFi, FreeRTOS scheduling,
LittleFS flash operations, and the bootloader applying an image.
